        <h1>LeetCode 877: Stone Game (C++)</h1>
        <div class="problem-description">
            <p><strong>Problem:</strong>
                Alice and Bob play a game with piles of stones arranged in a row. On each turn, a player takes the
                entire pile from either the beginning or the end of the row, and the piles are added to that player's
                score. Alice starts first, and both players play optimally. Given an even number of piles, always
                positive, and total stones odd (no ties possible), return true if Alice wins the game.
            </p>
            <p><strong>Example:</strong>
                Input: piles = [5,3,4,5]<br>
                Output: true<br>
                Explanation: Alice can always win by choosing piles strategically. For example, Alice starts with 5,
                forces Bob into a losing position, and ends up with a higher total score.
            </p>
        </div>
        <div class="code-container">
            <button class="copy-button" onclick="copyCode(this)">Copy Code</button>
            <pre><code class="language-cpp">class Solution {
public:
    bool stoneGame(vector&lt;int&gt;&amp; arr) {
        int sz = arr.size();
        vector&lt;int&gt; best = arr;
        for (int width = 2; width &lt;= sz; width++) {
            for (int start = 0; start &lt;= sz - width; start++) {
                int end = start + width - 1;
                best[start] = max(
                    arr[start] - best[start + 1],
                    arr[end] - best[start]
                );
            }
        }
        return best[0] &gt; 0;
    }
};</code></pre>
